### Topic 65 - Distributed tracing (VS Code "REST Client")
### Start: docker compose up -d (Zipkin), payment-service (8082), order-service (8081).

@order = http://localhost:8081

### 1. Place an order - the response contains the traceId. Compare it with BOTH consoles.
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item": "Pizza Margherita", "amount": 450.0 }

### 2. Same, but WE choose the correlation id (look for it in both consoles)
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
correlation-id: checkout-42

{ "item": "Gaming Laptop", "amount": 75000.0 }

### 3. Continue an EXISTING trace (what an upstream service would send) - W3C traceparent header
###    format: version-traceId(32 hex)-parentSpanId(16 hex)-flags
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
traceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01

{ "item": "Coffee", "amount": 120.0 }

### 4. Current trace/span ids from Java code
GET {{order}}/api/orders/trace-info

### 5. Invalid order - see the error recorded on the span in Zipkin
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item": "", "amount": 0 }

### 6. Zipkin API: last traces of order-service (UI: http://localhost:9411)
GET http://localhost:9411/api/v2/traces?serviceName=order-service&limit=5
